Hello {!Contact.FirstName},

Arizona State University participates in the Western Undergraduate Exchange (WUE); a program coordinated by the Western Interstate Commission for Higher Education (WICHE). Students in a WUE program only pay 150 percent of Arizona base resident tuition plus all applicable fees for fall and spring terms. Check out details at the following site: https://students.asu.edu/admission/wue

In order to qualify for this reduced tuition, students must meet the following criteria:

  - Students must be a permanent resident of Alaska, California, Colorado, Hawaii, Idaho,              Montana, Nevada, New Mexico, North Dakota, Oregon, South Dakota, Utah, Washington, Wyoming or residents of the Commonwealth of the Northern Mariana Islands.
  - Students must apply to one of the ASU WUE-eligible majors or programs - check to see if your major or program applies: https://webapp4.asu.edu/programs/t5/programs/Keyword/wue/undergrad/false
  - Transfer students must have an overall GPA of 2.50 or higher on a 4.00 scale in all transferable course work.
  - Community college transfer students must have an associate degree or 60 transferable credit hours (BAS degree programs are only open to students who have an AAS or equivalent degree).

Students who enroll in one of these majors and meet the eligibility requirements will automatically receive the discounted tuition. No separate application is required.

Let me know if you have any additional questions about the admission process.

{!User.Recruiter_Full_Name__c}
Admission Services
{!User.Recruiter_Title__c}
{!User.Recruiter_Email__c}
{!User.Recruiter_Phone__c}

